<title>GERMANY: Thyssen sells unit to 3i, others.</title>
<headline>Thyssen sells unit to 3i, others.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German engineering and steel giant Thyssen AG said on Tuesday it had sold its Hommelwerke GmbH unit to a group including British investment company 3i Group Plc.</p>
<p>In addition to 3i, Stuttgart-based Gesellschaft fuer Vermoegensverwaltung und Beteiligung mbH and Hommelwerke's own management, were in the buying group.</p>
<p>Hommelwerke has sales of 40 million marks and specialises in the production of measurement instruments. Thyssen said the sale, which was backdated to take effect from October 1 last year, was part of its portfolio-cleansing strategy.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
